.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
node_modules/

# ---- current build note (2026-08-07) ----
#
# This snapshot is the CDN build: the pages load supabase-js and xlsx
# from cdn.jsdelivr.net / cdn.sheetjs.com at pinned versions, and
# script-src names those two origins. So vendor/ and vendor-lock.json
# do not exist here and there is nothing for the section below to
# track — it is kept because it becomes true again the moment
# sync-vendor.js is run and the self-hosted pages are adopted.

# ---- what is deliberately NOT ignored ----
#
# vendor/ and vendor-lock.json are TRACKED, on purpose.
#
# vendor/ holds supabase-js and xlsx, served from this origin so
# script-src can stay 'self' alone. Ignoring them would mean the
# deployed site is missing the two files every page depends on, and the
# symptom is a portal that renders and then does nothing at all.
#
# vendor-lock.json is the record of which bytes were vetted. Committing
# the libraries without it leaves nothing to check them against, which
# is most of the point — see sync-vendor.js.

# ---- not in this repo, and needs to be ----
#
# Three Supabase Edge Functions are invoked by name from the client and
# have no source here:
#
#   notify-approval    approval.js  — approval/rejection emails
#   admin-delete-user  approval.js  — wraps admin_delete_user_data()
#                                     plus the Auth Admin API, neither
#                                     of which belongs in the browser
#   ai-assistant       page-dashboard.js — presumably the only caller
#                                     of ai_assistant_take_token()
#
# They are not ignored; they were never added. A deploy from this repo
# alone produces a portal where approval emails silently fail, deleting
# a user throws, and the assistant is dead — three separate faults that
# do not look related and none of which point here.
#
# They live in supabase/functions/<name>/index.ts. Add them, or write
# down where they are kept instead.
